A maintainer on the project DarioHuesoGisbert/bonsai (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #11: Implement Commit concrete class (history as a Merkle DAG)

## Overview

Implement `Commit`, the third concrete object type in the bonsai Git-like project (namespace `bonsai::objects`). A commit records "this tree is now the state of the repository": it points to a `Tree` by hash, optionally to parent `Commit`(s) by hash, plus author metadata and a message. With it, the object model becomes a real Merkle DAG — a commit's identity chains the identities of its tree and parents, making history tamper-evident and content-addressed, enabling `git log` / `git checkout` (Phases 3–4).

## Use Cases

- Create an initial commit with a tree id, author, message, and no parents.
- Add parents one at a time (oldest first) via `add_parent` during assembly.
- Serialize commits canonically and derive deterministic content-addressed IDs.
- Walk parent chains by hash; changing anything anywhere in history changes the hash of every descendant commit.

## Serialization Format (canonical)

After the `"commit <len>\0"` header (same convention as Blob/Tree; `<len>` is body byte count excluding the header), the body is:

```
tree <hex tree id>\n
[parent <hex parent id>\n]   (repeated once per parent, only if any)
author <name> <email>\n
\n
<message>
```

- Tree line mandatory and first.
- Parent lines only appear if parents exist; initial commit has none.
- No timestamps or timezone (deliberate bonsai simplification for determinism — "same content, same identity"). If timestamps are wanted later, add an explicit `std::string timestamp` field — do **not** invent a default.
- Message separated from header block by `\n\n`; empty message still ends with `author ...\n\n`.
- IDs rendered lowercase hex via `Sha256::hex()`; the commit is hashed over those exact bytes.
- Example with tree `T`, parent `P`, author `A B <a@b>`, message `hi`:
  ```
  tree T
  parent P
  author A B <a@b>

  hi
  ```

## Required Public API

```cpp
namespace bonsai::objects {

struct Author {
    std::string name;
    std::string email;
};

class Commit : public Object {
public:
    Commit(bonsai::hash::Sha256 tree_id, Author author, std::string message);

    // Parents added one at a time, in chronological order (oldest first).
    void add_parent(bonsai::hash::Sha256 parent_id);

    [[nodiscard]] std::string type() const override;                          // "commit"
    [[nodiscard]] std::vector<std::byte> serialize() const override;

    [[nodiscard]] const bonsai::hash::Sha256& tree_id() const noexcept;
    [[nodiscard]] std::span<const bonsai::hash::Sha256> parents() const noexcept;
    [[nodiscard]] const std::string& author_name() const noexcept;
    [[nodiscard]] const std::string& author_email() const noexcept;
    [[nodiscard]] const std::string& message() const noexcept;

private:
    bonsai::hash::Sha256 tree_id_;
    std::vector<bonsai::hash::Sha256> parents_;
    Author author_;
    std::string message_;
};

}  // namespace bonsai::objects
```

Signatures may be refined, but keep: `Commit` is an `Object`; tree line mandatory and first; parents a list; no timestamps; serialization matches the canonical format.

## Acceptance Criteria

- `Commit` inherits from `Object`, overrides `type()` (`"commit"`) and `serialize()`.
- Constructor requires tree id, author, message; parents start empty.
- `add_parent(...)` appends; multiple calls append multiple parents.
- `serialize()` emits canonical `"commit <len>\0<body>"` with exact line structure.
- Initial commit (no parents) has no parent lines; a commit with parents includes one `parent <hex>` line per parent.
- Two commits with same tree/author/parents/message produce equal `id()` (determinism, Template Method via `Object::id()`).
- Changing message, tree id, or a parent produces a different `id()`.
- Chain works: `commit2.parents()[0] == commit1.id()` and `commit2` hashes differently from `commit1`.
- Accessors are `const`, return non-owning views (`span` / `const&`); no mutation after construction except `add_parent` during assembly.
- No raw `new`/`delete`; RAII containers and value types only.
- Clean build with `/W4` (MSVC) and `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion` (gcc/clang).
- GoogleTest covers the above cases; CI green on Ubuntu.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

```jac
"""Bonsai Merkle DAG: content-addressed commits linked by parent edges; HistoryLogger walks the chain."""

node Tree {
    has label: str = "";
    has hex_id: str = "";
}

edge Parent { }

node Commit {
    has tree_id: str = "";
    has author_name: str = "";
    has author_email: str = "";
    has message: str = "";
    has object_id: str = "";
    has parent_hexes: list[str] = [];

    def hex_digest(raw: str) -> str {
        n = 0;
        for ch in raw {
            n = (n * 33 + ord(ch)) % 4294967296;
        }
        return f"{n:08x}";
    }

    def body_bytes() -> str {
        body = f"tree {self.tree_id}";
        for ph in self.parent_hexes {
            body = f"{body}\nparent {ph}";
        }
        body = f"{body}\nauthor {self.author_name} <{self.author_email}>\n\n{self.message}";
        return body;
    }

    def finalize() -> None {
        body = self.body_bytes();
        header = f"commit {len(body)}";
        self.object_id = self.hex_digest(f"{header}\0{body}");
    }

    def add_parent(parent: Commit) -> None {
        self +>:Parent:+> parent;
        self.parent_hexes.append(parent.object_id);
    }
}

walker HistoryLogger {
    has seen: list[str] = [];
    has depth: int = 0;

    can walk with Commit entry {
        if here.object_id and here.object_id in self.seen {
            print("[cycle-guard] stopping — parent chain loops");
            disengage;
        }
        if here.object_id {
            self.seen.append(here.object_id);
        }
        pad = "";
        for _ in range(self.depth) {
            pad = f"{pad}  ";
        }
        oid = here.object_id if here.object_id else "(pending)";
        print(f"{pad}{oid} | {here.message}");
        self.depth += 1;
        visit [->:Parent:->] else { disengage; };
        self.depth -= 1;
    }
}

walker ParentAuditor {
    has collected: list[str] = [];
    has skip_self: bool = True;

    can audit with Commit entry {
        if self.skip_self {
            self.skip_self = False;
            visit [->:Parent:->] else { disengage; };
        } else {
            self.collected.append(here.object_id);
            visit [-->];
        }
    }
}

with entry {
    t1 = Tree(label="root-fs", hex_id="d4e5f6a1b2c3d4e5");
    t2 = Tree(label="add-readme", hex_id="e5f6a1b2c3d4e5f6");
    t3 = Tree(label="fix-typo", hex_id="f6a1b2c3d4e5f6a1");

    c1 = Commit(
        tree_id=t1.hex_id,
        author_name="Ada Lovelace",
        author_email="ada@bonsai.dev",
        message="Initial commit"
    );
    c1.finalize();

    c2 = Commit(
        tree_id=t2.hex_id,
        author_name="Ada Lovelace",
        author_email="ada@bonsai.dev",
        message="Add README"
    );
    c2.add_parent(c1);
    c2.finalize();

    c3 = Commit(
        tree_id=t3.hex_id,
        author_name="Ada Lovelace",
        author_email="ada@bonsai.dev",
        message="Fix typo in README"
    );
    c3.add_parent(c2);
    c3.finalize();

    root ++> c3;

    print("=== canonical serialize (c2) ===");
    print(c2.body_bytes());
    print("================================");

    twin = Commit(
        tree_id=t1.hex_id,
        author_name="Ada Lovelace",
        author_email="ada@bonsai.dev",
        message="Initial commit"
    );
    twin.finalize();
    print(f"deterministic ids: {twin.object_id == c1.object_id}");

    twin.message = "Tweaked message";
    twin.finalize();
    print(f"message change alters id: {twin.object_id != c1.object_id}");

    print(f"parent chain link: {c3.parent_hexes[0] == c2.object_id}");
    print(f"c1 != c2 identity: {c1.object_id != c2.object_id}");

    auditor = ParentAuditor();
    c3 spawn auditor;
    chain_ok = False;
    if len(auditor.collected) > 0 {
        chain_ok = auditor.collected[0] == c2.object_id;
    }
    print(f"walker parent audit: {chain_ok}");

    print("=== git log (newest first) ===");
    c3 spawn HistoryLogger();
}
```

"""Weather sweep: walk weather stations, report each reading, then summarize min and max."""

node WeatherStation {
    has location: str = "";
    has celsius: float = 0.0;
}

walker WeatherSweep {
    has readings: list[float] = [];

    def report_summary() {
        if len(self.readings) == 0 {
            print("All readings: []");
            print("Min: none, Max: none");
            return;
        }
        lo = self.readings[0];
        hi = self.readings[0];
        for t in self.readings {
            if t < lo {
                lo = t;
            }
            if t > hi {
                hi = t;
            }
        }
        print(f"All readings: {self.readings}");
        print(f"Min: {lo}, Max: {hi}");
    }

    can start with Root entry {
        visit [--> ] else {
            self.report_summary();
            disengage;
        }
    }

    can sweep with WeatherStation entry {
        print(f"{here.location}: {here.celsius} C");
        self.readings.append(here.celsius);
        visit [--> ] else {
            self.report_summary();
            disengage;
        }
    }
}

with entry {
    root ++> WeatherStation(location="Boston", celsius=12.5)
        ++> WeatherStation(location="Miami", celsius=28.3)
        ++> WeatherStation(location="Denver", celsius=5.1)
        ++> WeatherStation(location="Phoenix", celsius=35.7);
    root spawn WeatherSweep();
}

