A maintainer on the project alanua/Skeleton (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #2278: Implement private Gewerbe Legal cross-domain case flow with Google/Microsoft adapters

Parent: #2267
Related: #2266
Priority: P0 cross-domain integration
Privacy Boundary: PRIVATE_CASE_DATA_OUTSIDE_PUBLIC_GITHUB; public issue contains schema/adapter requirements only.

Goal:
Implement the first real private cross-domain case flow for Gewerbe Legal without placing personal/legal/email/account content in GitHub.

Target flow:
Mail provider (Gmail or Microsoft mail) -> MailDomain -> private Gewerbe Legal Case -> correspondence index -> Documents refs -> Skeleton Scheduler canonical deadlines/checkpoints -> optional Google Calendar/Microsoft Calendar human mirrors -> Telegram/Jeeves alerts/actions -> reply drafting/approval -> provider send path when separately authorized.

Required architecture:
- Skeleton Scheduler is canonical for operational tasks, dependencies, retries, follow-ups and deadline state.
- Google Calendar / Microsoft Calendar are user-facing calendar mirrors/adapters, not competing canonical schedulers.
- Calendar mirror events carry stable Skeleton refs and are idempotent; edits/conflicts are reconciled according to explicit authority policy.
- Gmail and Microsoft mail are provider adapters behind the same MailDomain contract.
- Google Drive and OneDrive are document-store adapters behind the same private Documents domain contract where appropriate; no provider becomes the domain model.
- Gmail/Google Calendar/Drive and Microsoft Mail/Calendar/OneDrive credentials use the Secret Store / machine identity route; no tokens in GitHub/issues/logs.
- private case values, names, amounts, courts, addresses, message bodies and attachments remain private; public GitHub records only aggregate/public-safe implementation state.

First canary behavior:
- create a private legal case with three private Scheduler checkpoints sourced from an existing correspondence thread;
- re-check the thread at each checkpoint through the correct mail adapter;
- derive whether response is substantive/holding/no-response through local-first LLM/classifier with safe fallback;
- keep the canonical deadline state in Skeleton Scheduler;
- mirror only human-useful deadline markers to calendar;
- notify in Telegram only when actionable/NEEDS_OPERATOR per policy;
- offer `Підготувати відповідь` for important correspondence and use the Ukrainian-approval -> source-language render workflow from #2266;
- attachments/documents route by private reference to Documents/Drive/OneDrive as configured.

Provider scope:
1. Google: Gmail, Google Calendar, Google Drive.
2. Microsoft: Microsoft/Outlook mail, Microsoft Calendar, OneDrive.

Implementation order:
1. audit existing Google connector/adapters and current Skeleton Scheduler/MemoryGateway private routes;
2. define provider-neutral Mail/Calendar/Document adapter interfaces;
3. implement/bridge Google adapters;
4. implement/bridge Microsoft adapters using Graph-compatible/provider API route;
5. implement private case bridge and idempotent calendar mirror policy;
6. live-safe canary with synthetic/private refs only in public receipts.

Success criteria:
- one private Gewerbe Legal case can ingest from either Gmail or Microsoft mail;
- Skeleton Scheduler remains canonical and continues autonomously without ChatGPT Scheduler;
- Google/Microsoft calendar mirrors do not duplicate tasks or become competing authorities;
- OneDrive/Drive refs can be attached to the same private case/document graph;
- Telegram actions and reply workflow work provider-independently;
- no private case data leaks to public GitHub.

Forbidden:
- no private legal data in issue/PR/test fixtures;
- no separate Google-only or Microsoft-only scheduler/control plane;
- no direct provider-specific business logic outside adapters/registries;
- no autonomous external email send until send policy is explicitly authorized.

Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.

"""Private Gewerbe Legal cross-domain case flow demo.

Models the essential scenario from issue #2278: a private legal case pulls
checkpoints from Skeleton Scheduler (canonical), mirrors a human deadline to
a calendar adapter, fetches correspondence via a provider-neutral mail
adapter, and routes reply/notification actions. The walker traverses the
private case graph end-to-end and reports what is actionable.
"""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider-neutral adapter contracts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

edge IngestsFrom {
    # mail provider -> MailDomain (Gmail or Microsoft)
    has provider_name: str = "";
}

edge MirrorTarget {
    # canonical -> calendar mirror (Google or Microsoft)
    has provider_name: str = "";
}

edge DocumentStore {
    # case -> Documents ref (Drive or OneDrive)
    has provider_name: str = "";
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Domain entities
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

node MailDomain {
    # Mail provider adapter (Gmail / Microsoft) behind one contract.
    has provider_name: str = "";
    has thread_id: str = "";
}

node SchedulerCheckpoint {
    # Skeleton Scheduler = canonical deadline/follow-up owner.
    has title: str = "";
    has deadline_iso: str = "";
    has status: str = "open";
}

node CalendarMirror {
    # User-facing mirror ONLY. Carries a stable skeleton ref so edits are
    # idempotent and never become a competing authority.
    has provider_name: str = "";
    has mirror_label: str = "";
    has skeleton_ref: str = "";
}

node DocumentRef {
    # Drive / OneDrive ref attached to the case graph.
    has provider_name: str = "";
    has doc_label: str = "";
}

node LegalCase {
    # The private case. Holds ONLY public-safe structural state.
    has case_id: str = "";
    has domain: str = "Gewerbe Legal";
    has reply_offered: bool = False;
    has needs_operator: bool = False;
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Walker: walk a private legal case end-to-end and report actionable state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

walker CaseAuditor {
    has checkpoints_seen: int = 0;
    has mirror_checked: bool = False;
    has mail_pulled: bool = False;
    has docs_attached: int = 0;

    can start with Root entry {
        print(f"Auditing private case flow on root");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can audit_case with LegalCase entry {
        print(f"[CASE {here.case_id}] domain={here.domain} "
              f"reply_offered={here.reply_offered} "
              f"needs_operator={here.needs_operator}");
        # Walk every typed relationship out of the case.
        visit [->:IngestsFrom:->];
        visit [->:MirrorTarget:->];
        visit [->:DocumentStore:->];
    }

    can audit_mail with MailDomain entry {
        self.mail_pulled = True;
        print(f"[MAIL] provider={here.provider_name} "
              f"thread={here.thread_id} (adapter pulled)");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can audit_checkpoint with SchedulerCheckpoint entry {
        self.checkpoints_seen += 1;
        state = "ACTIONABLE" if here.status == "open" else "CLOSED";
        print(f"[CHECKPOINT {state}] {here.title} deadline={here.deadline_iso}");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can audit_mirror with CalendarMirror entry {
        self.mirror_checked = True;
        print(f"[CAL MIRROR] provider={here.provider_name} "
              f"label={here.mirror_label} ref={here.skeleton_ref} "
              f"(idempotent, non-canonical)");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can audit_doc with DocumentRef entry {
        self.docs_attached += 1;
        print(f"[DOC] provider={here.provider_name} label={here.doc_label}");
        visit [-->];
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Walker: depend on the mail provider through the neutral contract.
# Cycles are guarded by an explicit visited set on the walker; jac 0.36
# walkers do NOT dedupe visits automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

walker ReplyDrafter {
    has visited_ids: list[str] = [];
    has drafted: bool = False;

    can start with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can draft with LegalCase entry {
        case_tag = f"case::{here.case_id}";
        if case_tag in self.visited_ids {
            return;
        }
        self.visited_ids.append(case_tag);
        if here.reply_offered {
            self.drafted = True;
            print(f"[REPLY] Ukrainian approval prepared for case "
                  f"{here.case_id}; source-language render pending "
                  f"explicit send authorization");
        } else {
            print(f"[REPLY] case {here.case_id}: no important "
                  f"correspondence, no draft needed");
        }
        visit [-->];
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo wiring
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

with entry {
    # Two canary cases: one ingested from Gmail, one from Microsoft mail.
    case_g = LegalCase(
        case_id="GL-0001",
        reply_offered=True,
        needs_operator=True
    );
    case_m = LegalCase(
        case_id="GL-0002",
        reply_offered=False,
        needs_operator=False
    );

    # --- Gmail path --------------------------------------------------------
    gmail = MailDomain(provider_name="Gmail", thread_id="gmail-thread-A1");
    case_g +>:IngestsFrom(provider_name="Gmail"):+> gmail;

    cp_g1 = SchedulerCheckpoint(title="Acknowledge receipt", deadline_iso="2025-02-01");
    cp_g2 = SchedulerCheckpoint(title="Request evidence", deadline_iso="2025-02-10");
    cp_g3 = SchedulerCheckpoint(title="File response", deadline_iso="2025-02-20");
    case_g ++> cp_g1 ++> cp_g2 ++> cp_g3;

    gcal = CalendarMirror(
        provider_name="Google Calendar",
        mirror_label="GL-0001 / File response",
        skeleton_ref="sched:cp_g3"
    );
    case_g +>:MirrorTarget(provider_name="Google Calendar"):+> gcal;

    gdrive = DocumentRef(provider_name="Google Drive", doc_label="evidence.pdf");
    case_g +>:DocumentStore(provider_name="Google Drive"):+> gdrive;

    # --- Microsoft path ----------------------------------------------------
    ms = MailDomain(provider_name="Microsoft", thread_id="ms-thread-B7");
    case_m +>:IngestsFrom(provider_name="Microsoft"):+> ms;

    cp_m1 = SchedulerCheckpoint(title="Initial review", deadline_iso="2025-03-01");
    cp_m2 = SchedulerCheckpoint(title="Operator check-in", deadline_iso="2025-03-15");
    case_m ++> cp_m1 ++> cp_m2;

    mcal = CalendarMirror(
        provider_name="Microsoft Calendar",
        mirror_label="GL-0002 / Operator check-in",
        skeleton_ref="sched:cp_m2"
    );
    case_m +>:MirrorTarget(provider_name="Microsoft Calendar"):+> mcal;

    onedrive = DocumentRef(provider_name="OneDrive", doc_label="intake.docx");
    case_m +>:DocumentStore(provider_name="OneDrive"):+> onedrive;

    # Mount both cases on root and run the auditors.
    root ++> case_g ++> case_m;

    root spawn CaseAuditor();
    print("---");
    root spawn ReplyDrafter();
}

"""Commit gate demo with typed plugin dependencies, exact checks, and cycle detection."""

node Plugin {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has plugin_id: str = "";
    has version: str = "";
    has referenced: bool = False;
}

node CommitOperation {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has phase: str = "COMMIT_PREPARED";
    has candidate_fresh: bool = True;
    has active_tree_valid: bool = True;
    has configuration_valid: bool = True;
    has projection_valid: bool = True;
    has reference_valid: bool = True;
    has rollback_required: bool = False;
    has raw_candidate_hash: str = "";
    has raw_tree_hash: str = "";
}

node Gate {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has durable: bool = True;
    has acknowledged: bool = True;
    has released: bool = False;
    has shell_instance: str = "";
    has rescan_generation: int = 0;
}

edge HasCandidate { }
edge HasGate { }
edge DependsOn {
    has relation: str = "required";
}

walker CommitAuditor {
    has seen_plugin_ids: list[str] = [];
    has cycle_count: int = 0;

    can start with Root entry {
        print("Starting gated commit audit");
        visit [-->] else {
            disengage;
        }
    }

    can inspect_operation with CommitOperation entry {
        candidate_status = "fresh" if here.candidate_fresh else "stale";
        tree_status = "valid" if here.active_tree_valid else "stale";
        config_status = "valid" if here.configuration_valid else "stale";
        projection_status = "valid" if here.projection_valid else "stale";
        reference_status = "valid" if here.reference_valid else "stale";
        rollback_status = "required" if here.rollback_required else "not-required";

        print(f"{here.phase}: candidate={candidate_status}, "
              f"tree={tree_status}, config={config_status}, "
              f"projection={projection_status}, reference={reference_status}, "
              f"rollback={rollback_status}");
        print(f"evidence candidate={here.raw_candidate_hash}, "
              f"tree={here.raw_tree_hash}");

        visit [->:HasCandidate:->] else {
            disengage;
        }
    }

    can inspect_plugin with Plugin entry {
        if here.plugin_id in self.seen_plugin_ids {
            self.cycle_count += 1;
            print(f"dependency cycle detected at {here.plugin_id}");
        } else {
            self.seen_plugin_ids.append(here.plugin_id);
            reference_status = "referenced" if here.referenced else "unreferenced";
            print(f"plugin {here.plugin_id} {here.version}: {reference_status}");
            visit [->:DependsOn:->] else {
                disengage;
            }
        }
    }

    can inspect_gate with Gate entry {
        gate_status = "released" if here.released else "held";
        acknowledgement = "acknowledged" if here.acknowledged else "missing";
        print(f"gate {gate_status}, shell={here.shell_instance}, "
              f"rescan={here.rescan_generation}, {acknowledgement}");
    }
}

with entry {
    operation = CommitOperation(
        title="O-8 commit",
        phase="RELEASE_PENDING",
        candidate_fresh=True,
        active_tree_valid=True,
        configuration_valid=True,
        projection_valid=True,
        reference_valid=True,
        raw_candidate_hash="candidate:91af",
        raw_tree_hash="tree:44c2"
    );

    candidate = Plugin(
        title="candidate plugin",
        plugin_id="weather",
        version="2.0",
        referenced=True
    );

    dependency_a = Plugin(
        title="loader dependency",
        plugin_id="loader",
        version="1.4"
    );

    dependency_b = Plugin(
        title="shared dependency",
        plugin_id="shared",
        version="3.1"
    );

    gate = Gate(
        title="durable unload gate",
        durable=True,
        acknowledged=True,
        released=False,
        shell_instance="shell-7",
        rescan_generation=12
    );

    root ++> operation;
    root +>:HasGate:+> gate;
    operation +>:HasCandidate:+> candidate;
    candidate +>:DependsOn(relation="required"):+> dependency_a;
    dependency_a +>:DependsOn(relation="required"):+> dependency_b;
    dependency_b +>:DependsOn(relation="required"):+> dependency_a;

    root spawn CommitAuditor();
}

"""Orchard maintenance: tour groves servicing pumps and sprinklers with a shared crew routine."""

node Device {
    has kind: str = "";
    has idle_hours: int = 0;
    has serviced: bool = False;
}

node Pump(Device) {
    has gpm: int = 0;
}

node Sprinkler(Device) {
    has radius_ft: int = 0;
}

node Grove {
    has grove_name: str = "";
}

walker Crew {
    has total_serviced: int = 0;

    can start with Root entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can tour with Grove entry {
        visit [-->];
    }

    can service with Pump | Sprinkler entry {
        label = "pump" if here.kind == "" else here.kind;
        print(f"Servicing {label}: idle {here.idle_hours}h -> reset");
        here.idle_hours = 0;
        here.serviced = True;
        self.total_serviced += 1;
    }

    can finish with Root exit {
        print(f"Total devices serviced: {self.total_serviced}");
    }
}

with entry {
    north = Grove(grove_name="North");
    south = Grove(grove_name="South");
    root ++> north ++> south;

    north ++> Pump(kind="drip", idle_hours=12, gpm=5);
    north ++> Sprinkler(kind="rotor", idle_hours=3, radius_ft=20);
    south ++> Pump(kind="submersible", idle_hours=8, gpm=12);
    south ++> Sprinkler(kind="impact", idle_hours=5, radius_ft=15);
    south ++> Pump(kind="centrifugal", idle_hours=20, gpm=30);

    root spawn Crew();
}

"""Sync relay model for browser persistent-worker chunk streaming.

Models the essential scenario from issue #1978: a browser tab routes a
large multi-chunk value through a persistent shared worker relay before
it reaches the server. The diagnostic surface (transport role, root
locator, chunk locator) is preserved on the failure node so tab versus
worker ownership is unambiguous when a chunk is unavailable.
"""

node Tab {
    has title: str = "";
    has transport_role: str = "browser-tab";
}

node Worker {
    has title: str = "";
    has transport_role: str = "persistent-shared-worker";
}

node Server {
    has title: str = "";
    has transport_role: str = "core";
}

node Chunk {
    has sequence: int = 0;
    has payload: str = "";
    has available: bool = True;
}

node Root {
    has locator: str = "";
    has available: bool = True;
}

edge SourcedFrom { }
edge Holds { }
edge Carries { }

walker Auditor {
    has visited: list[str] = [];

    can start with Server entry {
        self.visited.append(f"server:{here.title}");
        print(f"[server] role={here.transport_role} title={here.title}");
        visit [->:SourcedFrom:->];
    }

    can walk_workers with Worker entry {
        self.visited.append(f"worker:{here.title}");
        print(f"[worker] role={here.transport_role} title={here.title}");
        visit [->:SourcedFrom:->];
    }

    can walk_tabs with Tab entry {
        self.visited.append(f"tab:{here.title}");
        print(f"[tab] role={here.transport_role} title={here.title}");
        visit [->:Holds:->] else { visit [->:Carries:->]; }
    }

    can audit_chunks with Chunk entry {
        if not here.available {
            diag_role = "browser-tab";
            diag_locator = f"chunk#{here.sequence}";
            print(
                f"[FAIL] chunk unavailable | "
                f"transport_role={diag_role} "
                f"root_locator=root#{here.sequence} "
                f"chunk_locator={diag_locator}"
            );
        } else {
            print(f"[OK] chunk#{here.sequence} bytes={len(here.payload)}");
        }
    }
}

walker ControlMutation {
    can start with Server entry {
        print("[control] subsequent ordinary control mutation after stream");
        visit [->:SourcedFrom:->];
    }

    can propagate_worker with Worker entry {
        visit [->:SourcedFrom:->];
    }

    can propagate_tab with Tab entry {
        visit [->:Holds:->] else { visit [->:Carries:->]; }
    }

    can drop with Chunk entry {
        print(f"[control-drop] delivered chunk#{here.sequence} payload={here.payload}");
    }
}

with entry {
    server = Server(title="core");
    tab = Tab(title="MusicAgent-draft");
    worker = Worker(title="persistent-shared-worker");

    server +>:SourcedFrom:+> worker;
    worker +>:SourcedFrom:+> tab;

    c1 = Chunk(sequence=1, payload="alpha", available=True);
    c2 = Chunk(sequence=2, payload="beta", available=True);
    c3 = Chunk(sequence=3, payload="gamma", available=True);
    c4 = Chunk(sequence=4, payload="delta", available=False);
    c5 = Chunk(sequence=5, payload="epsilon", available=True);

    server +>:Holds:+> c1;
    server +>:Holds:+> c2;
    server +>:Holds:+> c3;
    server +>:Holds:+> c4;
    server +>:Holds:+> c5;

    tab +>:Holds:+> c1;
    tab +>:Holds:+> c2;
    tab +>:Holds:+> c3;
    tab +>:Holds:+> c4;
    tab +>:Holds:+> c5;

    worker +>:Carries:+> c1;
    worker +>:Carries:+> c2;
    worker +>:Carries:+> c3;
    worker +>:Carries:+> c4;
    worker +>:Carries:+> c5;

    print("=== audit: server -> worker -> tab -> chunks ===");
    server spawn Auditor();

    print("=== audit: subsequent control mutation after stream ===");
    control = Chunk(sequence=99, payload="control-mut", available=True);
    server +>:Holds:+> control;
    tab +>:Holds:+> control;
    worker +>:Carries:+> control;
    server spawn ControlMutation();
}

"""List-folder parity demo with typed containment edges and cycle-safe traversal."""

node ListFolder {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has folder_id: str = "";
    has deleted: bool = False;
}

node ListItem {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has list_id: str = "";
    has folder_id: str = "";
}

edge ContainsFolder: ListFolder --> ListFolder {
    has relation: str = "subfolder";
}

edge ContainsList: ListFolder --> ListItem {
    has relation: str = "assigned-list";
}

walker FolderAuditor {
    has seen_folders: list[str] = [];
    has audit_log: list[str] = [];
    has cycle_count: int = 0;
    has list_count: int = 0;
    has reports: list[list[str]] = [];

    can start with Root entry {
        self.audit_log.append("root: lists tree");
        visit [-->] else { disengage; }
    }

    can inspect_folder with ListFolder entry {
        if here.folder_id in self.seen_folders {
            self.cycle_count += 1;
            self.audit_log.append(f"cycle blocked at folder {here.title}");
            skip;
        } else {
            self.seen_folders.append(here.folder_id);
            self.audit_log.append(f"folder: {here.title}");
            visit [->:ContainsFolder:->] else {
                self.audit_log.append("no subfolders");
            }
            visit [->:ContainsList:->] else {
                self.audit_log.append("no lists");
            }
        }
    }

    can inspect_list with ListItem entry {
        self.list_count += 1;
        self.audit_log.append(f"list: {here.title} in {here.folder_id}");
    }

    can finish with Root exit {
        report self.audit_log;
    }
}

with entry {
    main = ListFolder(
        title="Reading",
        folder_id="folder-reading"
    );
    archive = ListFolder(
        title="Archive",
        folder_id="folder-archive"
    );
    deep = ListFolder(
        title="Deep research",
        folder_id="folder-deep"
    );
    favorites = ListItem(
        title="Favorites",
        list_id="list-favorites",
        folder_id="folder-archive"
    );
    references = ListItem(
        title="References",
        list_id="list-references",
        folder_id="folder-deep"
    );

    root ++> main;
    main +>:ContainsFolder(relation="subfolder"):+> archive;
    archive +>:ContainsFolder(relation="subfolder"):+> deep;
    archive +>:ContainsList(relation="list"):+> favorites;
    deep +>:ContainsList(relation="list"):+> references;

    # A stale move under a descendant creates a cycle; the guard blocks it.
    deep +>:ContainsFolder(relation="invalid move cycle"):+> archive;

    root spawn FolderAuditor();
}

